Vendored django-star-ratings
============================

This app is a trimmed copy of django-star-ratings 0.9.2
(https://github.com/wildfish/django-star-ratings, PyPI release
django-star-ratings 0.9.2), written by Wildfish and contributors. Upstream
is dormant, so the website carries the code it needs. It is distributed
under the license in LICENSE.

The app label, the models, their database tables and the migrations are
unchanged, so existing databases keep working. The swappable rating model
setting STAR_RATINGS_RATING_MODEL is still honoured.

Local modifications:

- Removed everything the website does not use: anonymous ratings, clearing
  a rating, deleting a rating by re-rating with the same score, the
  STAR_RATINGS_ANONYMOUS/CLEARABLE/RERATE/RERATE_SAME_DELETE/STAR_SPRITE/
  OBJECT_ID_PATTERN settings and their system check, the default widget
  template, the admin include template, the translations, the JavaScript
  sources, the Sass sources and the minified JavaScript bundle (the readable
  bundle static/star-ratings/js/star-ratings.js is served instead).
- Dropped the dependencies on django-model-utils, django-braces and
  swapper. UserRating.created/modified are plain DateTimeFields with
  auto_now_add/auto_now (also in migration 0001); the database columns are
  the same.
- The rater IP is no longer recorded; UserRating.ip stays in the schema and
  is NULL for new ratings. Upstream stored the X-Real-IP header, which is
  only trustworthy behind a proxy that overwrites it.
- The rate view only follows a "next" URL on the requesting host and
  rejects scores outside 1..STAR_RATINGS_RANGE.
- Dropped default_app_config and Python 2 leftovers; reformatted with
  black.
